# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# days/ is a submodule, not ignored -- see .gitmodules. It is a fork of
# iQua/days (origin: github.com/tj-0002/days) on branch
# feature/bmv2-integration, and it holds the integration itself:
#   days/src/p4/        the code
#   days/artifact/      the sixteen-scenario reproduction package
#
# It keeps its own history so upstream can still be merged and so the fork
# stays a fork, and this repository pins one commit of it. Work can continue in
# days/ without moving the pin; `git add days` in this repository is what moves
# it deliberately.
#
# The submodule is fetched over https so that a clone needs no ssh key. The
# local days/ checkout keeps its own ssh remote for pushing; the two are
# independent.
#
# behavioral-model: an upstream checkout and its install prefix, both rebuildable.
# docs/usage.md section 1.1 has the configure line.
bmv2-nolog/
bmv2-nolog-build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
experiments/bmv2-threadsafety/harness
*.o
*.so
__pycache__/

# Generated inputs -- regenerate with the script beside them
experiments/multicore/configs/
